.TH ROFI-SCREEN-TIME 1 "rofi-hub 0.2.1" "rofi-hub" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rofi-screen-time \- open the Screen Time Rofi UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rofi-screen-time
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rofi-screen-time
is a shell wrapper around
.BR "screen-time render \-\-format rofi" .
It resolves the terminal size, prepares the Rofi theme, and starts Rofi in
normal-window mode. Rofi re-invokes the wrapper for every script-mode step;
that path only runs the renderer.
.PP
The wrapper requires
.BR rofi
2.x. It reports a clean error when
.B screen-time
is missing from the same directory or when Rofi is not in
.BR PATH .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ROFI_BIN
Rofi executable. Defaults to
.BR rofi .
.TP
.B ROFI_THEME
Highest-precedence theme file.
.TP
.B ROFI_CONFIG
Explicit Rofi configuration file.
.TP
.B SCREEN_TIME_THEME
Screen Time theme file. Used after
.BR ROFI_THEME .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base for the per-user
.I screen-time/rofi/screen-time.rasi
theme.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_DIRS
System data directories searched after the user theme; defaults to
.IR /usr/local/share:/usr/share .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Base for the generated theme and Rofi PID file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/rofi/screen-time.rasi
Packaged Screen Time theme.
.TP
.I /usr/share/screen-time/rofi/screen-time.rasi
Alternative packaged theme location.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits with Rofi's status. Returns 127 when a required executable is missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR screen-time (1),
.BR rofi (1),
.BR rofi-hub (1)
